{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he comforted them and spoke to their heart.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: in these words of comfort he would say to them, Before you came down here people were murmuring about me, saying, 'He is a slave'; and through you it became known that I am a free man's son. And if I kill you, what will people say about me? 'A band of young men he found, called them brothers, and in the end killed them — does a man kill his brothers?' Another interpretation: Ten lamps could not extinguish one lamp; how then can one lamp extinguish ten lamps?"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:03.117487076Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}